{"qid":"visualpuzzles_00314","dataset":"visualpuzzles","question":"Each of the numbers 1,4,3,0 and 10 is written in one of the colored circles so that the sum of the numbers in the row is equal to the sum of the numbers in the column. Which number can be written in the pink circle?\nOptions:\nA: only 1\nB: only 10\nC: 1 or 3\nD: 4 or 10\nAnswer with the option's letter.","gold":"B","category":"algorithmic","generated_text":"Let's analyze the problem step by step.\n\nWe have 5 colored circles: blue, green, pink, yellow, and orange. The numbers to be placed are: 1, 4, 3, 0, and 10.\n\nThe arrangement is:\n\n    Blue\n  Green  Pink  Yellow\n    Orange\n\nThis forms a cross shape. The \"row\" is the horizontal line: Green, Pink, Yellow.\nThe \"column\" is the vertical line: Blue, Pink, Orange.\n\nThe condition is: sum of numbers in the row = sum of numbers in the column.\n\nLet\u2019s denote:\n- G = number in green circle\n- P = number in pink circle\n- Y = number in yellow circle\n- B = number in blue circle\n- O = number in orange circle\n\nThe row sum is: G + P + Y\nThe column sum is: B + P + O\n\nSet them equal:\nG + P + Y = B + P + O\n\nSubtract P from both sides:\nG + Y = B + O\n\nSo the sum of the green and yellow circles must equal the sum of the blue and orange circles.\n\nThe five numbers are: 1, 4, 3, 0, 10.\n\nWe need to assign each number to one circle such that G + Y = B + O.\n\nNote that the total sum of all five numbers is:\n1 + 4 + 3 + 0 + 10 = 18\n\nSince G + Y = B + O, and G + Y + B + O + P = 18, we can write:\n(G + Y) + (B + O) + P = 18\nBut G + Y = B + O, so:\n2*(G + Y) + P = 18\n\nTherefore, 2*(G + Y) = 18 - P\n\nSo (18 - P) must be even, which means P must be even.\n\nThe even numbers among the given are: 0 and 4.\n\nSo the pink circle must contain either 0 or 4.\n\nBut let's check if both are possible.\n\nWe need to assign the numbers 1, 3, 10, and the remaining two even numbers (0 or 4) to the other circles, such that G + Y = B + O.\n\nLet\u2019